& [DictatedIntent]
  + set up each work turn so the terms relevant to the larger job are included while generating the SOP that will govern performance of that job
  + prime the inference engine with terms that pin the useful trajectory from the beginning
  + compile lookahead and plan hints into SOP so execution encounters a wide paved road of useful cues and reaches the point faster
  + investigate whether this can make work three through five times faster without sacrificing correctness

& [SelectedName]
  + SOP Compiled Lookahead is the candidate feature name
  + a LookaheadPacket is the candidate bounded machine form compiled for one future inference horizon
  + PlanHints are attributed trajectory cues inside the packet and are never silently promoted to requirements facts authority or completed work

& [LookaheadCompiler]
  + inputs may include exact governing SOP identities current objective current repository or runtime state dependency graph last accepted receipts unresolved frontier feature-requirement matrix operational faults and the next bounded plan horizon
  + compiler selects the semantic terms meanings source anchors file and symbol coordinates identities likely operations expected outputs acceptance evidence refusal conditions and reentry cues most relevant to that horizon
  + output gives the next inference pass a dense navigable semantic launch surface so it spends less effort rediscovering vocabulary history location and success criteria
  + every included item retains source provenance class horizon owner validity condition and invalidation condition

& [LookaheadPacket]
  + GoverningAnchors repeat only exact imported requirements constraints identities and authority boundaries
  + SemanticPrimer names relevant vocabulary distinctions and relationships needed for the next work
  + CoordinatePrimer names expected repository paths symbols contracts artifacts receipts and evidence surfaces
  + TrajectorySpine orders the likely dependency path without claiming that predicted steps occurred
  + BranchHints state bounded if-observed-then-consider alternatives and preserve unresolved branches
  + EvidenceForecast names the gates receipts comparisons and refusal evidence likely needed for closure
  + FaultForecast names known operational and semantic failure modes that should be checked early
  + ReentryCue states what receipt or observation causes the next lookahead compilation
  + Invalidators name the state source authority result contradiction or drift that makes the packet stale

& [HorizonAndRecompilation]
  + immediate horizon may bind the next admissible operation strongly when current evidence makes it deterministic
  + near horizon may retain several conditional branches rather than forcing one premature route
  + distant horizon remains sparse and subordinate because detail there is more likely to become stale or create anchoring bias
  + every material receipt observation fault or changed authority may trigger invalidation and compilation of a new packet
  + execution must be able to leave the suggested road when evidence proves another in-scope route is necessary

& [AuthorityAndCognitionBoundary]
  + compiled lookahead is explicit recorded planning context and not hidden chain of thought model state K/V cache access truth proof permission or an impulse to act
  + a hint may reduce search but cannot authorize a tool call file edit process provider contact commit push installation activation or effect
  + external authority and current observations outrank derived hints
  + disagreement between a hint and evidence must preserve the evidence invalidate the hint and reopen planning
  + packets must not embed secrets private reasoning transient scratch unrelated conversation content or ungoverned foreign work

& [PerformanceHypothesis]
  + semantic priming may reduce repeated repository reads vocabulary reconstruction wrong-path tool calls plan reformulation and context spent restating known constraints
  + strongest acceleration is expected at repeated structured seams whose next coordinates evidence and failure modes are predictable
  + context overhead fixation stale assumptions and narrowed search may erase the benefit when packets are too large too certain or too distant
  + three through five times faster is an experiment target and not a current measured claim

& [MeasurementDirection]
  + compare equivalent work with and without compiled lookahead under the same model provider tool policy starting state task authority and resource ceilings
  + measure time to first correct action time to accepted closure input and output tokens tool calls redundant reads corrected-path changes gate failures unsupported assumptions and final requirement support
  + preserve quality safety and authority correspondence as non-regression gates rather than optimizing elapsed time alone
  + test several packet sizes and horizons so the result can select sparse moderate or wide priming instead of assuming more hints are always better

& [MetaphorTranslation]
  + the wide paved road is a high-signal inference trajectory with visible lane markers junction conditions destinations and stop signs
  + paving means compiling relevant semantic and operational coordinates before the turn begins
  + widening is appropriate at difficult junctions where several interdependent terms or evidence gates must remain jointly available
  + road construction remains subordinate to live terrain because observations can invalidate the predicted route

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical specification satisfaction signature prompt injection runtime integration model modification measurement claim autonomous execution provider use workspace mutation remote work FPGA Minecraft or physical effect is authorized
